{"parentUuid":"1b22756d-d7f4-4ad2-9914-9814f7473dda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4LkAFMNSKJ74M2ZwWLV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018XVXDVXBTNS5wZSG7d1MC7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/mike/nexus-wt/fix-mq5-main && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"test(cli): MQ-5 runner test asserts both layers now that MQ-6 verifies evidence on load\n\n#516 (verify on load) and #518 (identity binding) each passed alone; together an on-disk manifest edit is rejected as HASH_MISMATCH before identity is compared, turning main red. Assert the integrity rejection for the un-recorded edit, then the identity mismatch after an operator re-record (migrateLegacyRun).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git push -q -u origin v1/fix-mq5-main-red 2>&1 | tail -1; gh pr create --base main --title \"test(cli): fix main CI red from MQ-5 x MQ-6 interaction\" --body \"main CI failed on the merges of #518 and #517: \\`MQ-5 runner: a bound baseline run is IDENTITY_BOUND; an edited baseline manifest is INCOMPARABLE...\\` expected BASELINE_MANIFEST_MISMATCH but got HASH_MISMATCH. #516 verifies evidence on load, so an un-re-recorded edit is rejected before identity is compared. The test now asserts the integrity rejection, then the identity mismatch after an operator re-record. Test-only; 13/13 in the file locally.\n\nI merged #515-#518 and #520/#521 in one batch without waiting for main CI between them; this semantic conflict was not visible in either PR's own CI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" | tail -1","description":"Commit and open the main-red fix PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":496,"cache_read_input_tokens":253943,"output_tokens":811,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"serv